      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/nelson-last-minute-wedding-9.6996510?cmp=rss</guid>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/efd7a891-5df4-4785-b475-2854576d4f85,1764354862636/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C243%2C2048%2C1152%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A woman and a man look off to the right while standing outside among a creek and trees' width='620' height='349' title='Leah Fried and Tim Bowman are celebrating their nuptials — and the community that came together to make it all happen.'/><p>There is no story that encapsulates the vibes of Nelson, B.C., quite like this. Witnesses, a photographer, an officiant and a musician all showed up at Cottonwood Falls Park, with very little notice, to help an out-of-town couple’s dreams come true. </p>]]></description>
